course: dictionary
lesson: 13534
title: Words that link people to trouble
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Implicate» is a verb, a word for an action. It is about links: it shows that someone or something is connected to something wrong or to a problem. «The muddy footprints implicate Sam in the break-in.» Footprints are evidence, so they connect Sam to the break-in. That is what implicate means.
explain: Context clues help you find the meaning. Words like «evidence», «witness» and «suspect» tell you the text is about a crime. Words like «illnesses» and «problem» tell you it is about a cause. Ask: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word and check it still makes sense.
explain: The same word can work in a crime story and in health news. «Germs are implicated in the illness» means the germs are linked to the illness as a cause. Learn the common phrases too: be implicated in, implicate someone in a crime, evidence implicates. Phrases show you how a word is used.
fact: Implicate is a verb: implicate, implicates, implicated, implicating.
fact: «Implicate» means to show that someone is involved in something wrong, such as a crime.
fact: In a detective story, «The fingerprints implicate the gardener» means the clue links the gardener to the crime.
fact: «Implicate» can also mean to show that something is a cause or part of a problem, as in «smoking is implicated in many illnesses».
fact: A rarer, formal meaning is to imply or suggest something.
exercise: «The muddy footprints implicate Sam in the break-in.» What does implicate mean here? | Find a lost key | Wash the floor clean | *Show that Sam was involved in the break-in | Praise Sam for his help
exercise: Doctors say «Too much sugar is implicated in tooth decay.» What does implicated suggest? | Teeth are made of sugar | Sugar is sweet and tasty | *Sugar is linked as a cause of tooth decay | Sugar cures tooth decay
exercise: In a detective story, what does «evidence implicates» mean? | *The evidence points to someone being involved | The police lost all the evidence | The evidence is kept in a box | The evidence is always made of paper
test: «The witness implicated the stranger, who was seen near the bank.» What does implicated mean here? | Forgot | *Linked to a crime | Thanked | Ran away from
test: Yesterday the detective ___ two suspects in the theft. Which word fits? | *implicated | implicate | implicates | implicating
exam: «Germs were implicated in the outbreak of the illness.» What does implicated mean here? | Kept away from the school | *Linked as a cause of the illness | Counted and recorded carefully | Cured by the doctors
